{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/EVENTS.md && cat lib/analytics.dart'","aggregated_output":"# Product events — registration funnel\n\nOwner: product. Status: approved, waiting for implementation.\n\nWe want to see where people drop out between opening the app and reading the\noffers. Each row is one event. Names are snake_case and must match exactly,\ndashboards and funnels are already built on them.\n\n| Event | When | Properties |\n|---|---|---|\n| `registration_email_started` | User started typing their email | — |\n| `registration_phone_started` | User started typing their phone number | — |\n| `loan_amount_changed` | User moved the loan amount slider | `amount` (int, the chosen amount) |\n| `terms_accepted` | User ticked the terms and conditions checkbox | — |\n| `registration_continue_tapped` | User tapped Continue on the registration screen | `amount` (int), `terms` (bool) |\n| `offers_scrolled` | User scrolled the offers list | `offset` (double, how far they scrolled) |\n\nNotes\n- Do not send the email or the phone number as properties (PII).\n- Screen views are already tracked automatically, no event needed for those.\n- The funnel is: email started → phone started → amount changed → terms\n  accepted → continue tapped → offers scrolled.\nimport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\n/// Thin wrapper around PostHog so the key and host live in one place.\nclass Analytics {\n  static Future<void> init() async {\n    final config = PostHogConfig('phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI');\n    config.host = 'https://eu.i.posthog.com';\n    config.captureApplicationLifecycleEvents = true;\n    await Posthog().setup(config);\n  }\n\n  /// Sends one event. [props] is optional.\n  static Future<void> capture(String event, [Map<String, Object>? props]) =>\n      Posthog().capture(eventName: event, properties: props);\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat lib/screens/registration_screen.dart && cat lib/screens/offer_screen.dart'","aggregated_output":"import 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass RegistrationScreen extends StatefulWidget {\n  const RegistrationScreen({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  State<RegistrationScreen> createState() => _RegistrationScreenState();\n}\n\nclass _RegistrationScreenState extends State<RegistrationScreen> {\n  final _email = TextEditingController();\n  final _phone = TextEditingController();\n  double _amount = 50000;\n  bool _terms = false;\n\n  @override\n  void dispose() {\n    _email.dispose();\n    _phone.dispose();\n    super.dispose();\n  }\n\n  bool get _canContinue =>\n      _terms && _email.text.contains('@') && _phone.text.length >= 10;\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Scaffold(\n      appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('Register')),\n      body: Padding(\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16),\n        child: Column(\n          crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,\n          children: [\n            TextField(\n              controller: _email,\n              keyboardType: TextInputType.emailAddress,\n              decoration: const InputDecoration(labelText: 'Email'),\n              onChanged: (_) => setState(() {}),\n            ),\n            const SizedBox(height: 12),\n            TextField(\n              controller: _phone,\n              keyboardType: TextInputType.phone,\n              decoration: const InputDecoration(labelText: 'Phone'),\n              onChanged: (_) => setState(() {}),\n            ),\n            const SizedBox(height: 24),\n            Text('Loan amount: ${_amount.round()}'),\n            Slider(\n              min: 10000,\n              max: 500000,\n              divisions: 49,\n              value: _amount,\n              label: _amount.round().toString(),\n              onChanged: (v) => setState(() => _amount = v),\n            ),\n            CheckboxListTile(\n              value: _terms,\n              title: const Text('I accept the terms and conditions'),\n              controlAffinity: ListTileControlAffinity.leading,\n              onChanged: (v) => setState(() => _terms = v ?? false),\n            ),\n            const Spacer(),\n            FilledButton(\n              onPressed: _canContinue\n                  ? () => Navigator.of(context).pushNamed('/offers')\n                  : null,\n              child: const Text('Continue'),\n            ),\n          ],\n        ),\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nclass Offer {\n  const Offer(this.bank, this.months, this.rate);\n  final String bank;\n  final int months;\n  final double rate;\n}\n\nconst _offers = [\n  Offer('Norbank', 12, 9.9),\n  Offer('Norbank', 24, 10.4),\n  Offer('Fjordcredit', 12, 8.7),\n  Offer('Fjordcredit', 36, 11.2),\n  Offer('Vestkapital', 24, 9.5),\n  Offer('Vestkapital', 48, 12.0),\n  Offer('Sparbank', 12, 10.9),\n  Offer('Sparbank', 60, 12.8),\n  Offer('Nordlån', 36, 10.1),\n  Offer('Nordlån', 60, 12.3),\n];\n\nclass OfferScreen extends StatelessWidget {\n  const OfferScreen({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return Scaffold(\n      appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('Offers')),\n      body: ListView.builder(\n        itemCount: _offers.length,\n        itemBuilder: (context, i) {\n          final o = _offers[i];\n          return ListTile(\n            leading: const Icon(Icons.account_balance),\n            title: Text('${o.bank}, ${o.months} months'),\n            subtitle: Text('${o.rate.toStringAsFixed(1)}% APR'),\n            trailing: const Icon(Icons.chevron_right),\n            onTap: () {},\n          );\n        },\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
